        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(path): retain mise shims when MISE_DATA_DIR is blank",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where OpenClaw could omit the default mise shims directory from child-process PATH construction when MISE_DATA_DIR was set to whitespace.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nMISE_DATA_DIR is trimmed before selection, so a blank override behaves like an absent override and the existing home-directory default remains canonical.\n\n## User Impact\n\nCommands installed through mise remain discoverable when service environments contain a blank MISE_DATA_DIR value.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Base behavior: the regression could not find the default home/.local/share/mise/shims entry and failed with index -1.\n- Exact head b701ba021034ec68ed79c2379c2a8837d7ad64e0: focused regressions -> 2 passed, 20 skipped.\n- Command: node scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/infra/path-env.test.ts -- -t MISE_DATA_DIR\n- The test calls ensureOpenClawCliOnPath with a real candidate directory model and verifies the canonical default shim path is appended after system directories.\n- Targeted oxfmt check and git diff --check passed.\n\n\n\n\n### Real Windows production proof\n\nRan the current PR head on Windows with MISE_DATA_DIR set to whitespace and a real temporary home containing the default .local/share/mise/shims directory.\n\nObserved redacted output:\n\n- production ensureOpenClawCliOnPath appended the default shim directory: true\n- Windows where.exe resolved openclaw-proof.cmd from <temp-home>\\.local\\share\\mise\\shims\n- Windows cmd.exe executed the command through the bootstrapped PATH\n- real command output: OPENCLAW_MISE_LIVE\n- the temporary home and shim were removed after verification\n\nThis demonstrates real filesystem discovery, PATH propagation, executable resolution, and child execution rather than only the virtual-filesystem regression test.\n\r\n",
